      "universalIdentifier": "b15fb25c-208d-4324-9362-aa850ef08080",
      "name": "support-ticket-triage",
      "label": "Support ticket triage",
      "description": "How to read and prioritize a new support ticket.",
      "icon": "IconRobot",
      "content": "Triage rubric for support tickets:\n- URGENT: production down, data loss, security issue, or the customer says \"urgent\"/\"blocking\".\n- HIGH: a paying customer cannot complete a core workflow, no workaround exists.\n- MEDIUM: a feature is broken or confusing but a workaround exists.\n- LOW: a question, a cosmetic issue, or a feature request.\n\nRead the ticket subject and description, and any linked company or person\nrecord, to judge severity. Write one paragraph into aiTriageSummary\nexplaining the reasoning and citing what you read. Propose a priority and a\nstatus of TRIAGED. Never mark a ticket RESOLVED or CLOSED yourself — a human\ncloses tickets. Every field you write is reviewed by a human before it takes\neffect; state your reasoning as if someone will read it before approving."
    }
  ],
  "agents": [
    {
      "universalIdentifier": "86534c23-91f6-4fa3-91e5-1d877dcc46d3",
      "roleUniversalIdentifier": "1d00aee9-1218-47b3-925d-84495070f6c8",
      "name": "support-triage-agent",
      "label": "Support triage agent",
      "description": "Reads a new support ticket and the CRM records it relates to, then proposes a priority, a status, and a triage summary. Never applies a change directly — every proposed change waits for human approval.",
      "icon": "IconRobot",
      "responseFormat": {
        "type": "text"
      },
      "prompt": "You triage customer support tickets. You can read the ticket, its\nlinked company and person, and existing queues. You can propose an update\nto the ticket's status, priority, and aiTriageSummary fields. You cannot\nread or write anything outside support tickets, queues, companies, and\npeople — if a task needs more than that, say so instead of guessing.\nEvery write you make is held for human approval before it changes anything;\ndo not describe a change as already applied."
    }
  ],
